{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVJWqu4acFwiQgm3oXCw4P","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\"\n     2→\n     3→test.describe(\"LiveVite Dead View Tests\", () => {\n     4→  test(\"renders Vue component inside regular Phoenix controller view (dead view)\", async ({\n     5→    page,\n     6→  }) => {\n     7→    // Navigate to the dead view page\n     8→    const response = await page.goto(\"/dead-view\")\n     9→\n    10→    // First check if the page loaded successfully (no 500 error)\n    11→    expect(response.status()).toBe(200)\n    12→\n    13→    // Verify the server-rendered content from the controller\n    14→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-server-message]\")).toHaveText(\"Hello from dead view!\")\n    15→\n    16→    // Wait for Vue to initialize and hydrate the component\n    17→    // In dead views, Vue still mounts via the VueHook initialization\n    18→    await page.waitForTimeout(500)\n    19→\n    20→    // Verify the Vue component rendered correctly\n    21→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-dead-view]\")).toBeVisible()\n    22→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-vue-message]\")).toHaveText(\"Hello from dead view!\")\n    23→  })\n    24→})\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2zmZWMogU2W6S6B8JQeo3","session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"179a0282-ab68-4bb3-b996-36fc5a37c1c2"}
