{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxZCp4SY3SwpDkeLYmJHoa","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.DeadViewHTML do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  HTML view module for dead view tests.\n     4→  \"\"\"\n     5→  use Phoenix.Component\n     6→  use LiveVite\n     7→\n     8→  def show(assigns) do\n     9→    ~H\"\"\"\n    10→    <h1>Dead View Test</h1>\n    11→    <p data-pw-server-message>{@message}</p>\n    12→\n    13→    <.vue message={@message} v-component=\"dead-view/dead-view-test\" id=\"dead-view-component\" />\n    14→    \"\"\"\n    15→  end\n    16→end\n    17→\n    18→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.DeadViewController do\n    19→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n    20→  A regular Phoenix controller (not LiveView) to test Vue components in dead views.\n    21→  \"\"\"\n    22→  use Phoenix.Controller, formats: [:html]\n    23→\n    24→  def show(conn, _params) do\n    25→    conn\n    26→    |> put_layout(html: {LiveVite.E2E.Layout, :live})\n    27→    |> Plug.Conn.assign(:message, \"Hello from dead view!\")\n    28→    |> render(:show)\n    29→  end\n    30→end\n    31→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2zmZWMogU2W6S6B8JQeo3","session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"18236e98-7f0d-4311-80ad-6b3075d8dc7f"}
