{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015CJpPa99CUWQVbGukvTBpC","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\"\n     2→import { syncLV, evalLV } from \"../../utils.js\"\n     3→\n     4→test.describe(\"useEventReply E2E Tests\", () => {\n     5→  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n     6→    await page.goto(\"/event-reply-test\")\n     7→    await syncLV(page)\n     8→  })\n     9→\n    10→  test(\"component initializes correctly\", async ({ page }) => {\n    11→    // Verify component is mounted\n    12→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-event-reply-test]\")).toBeVisible()\n    13→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-server-counter]\")).toHaveText(\"Server Counter: 0\")\n    14→\n    15→    // Initial state should be empty\n    16→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-loading]\")).toHaveText(\"Loading: false\")\n    17→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-data]\")).toHaveText(\"Data: null\")\n    18→  })\n    19→\n    20→  test(\"increment event with reply works correctly\", async ({ page }) => {\n    21→    // Click increment by 1\n    22→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-1]\").click()\n    23→    await syncLV(page)\n    24→\n    25→    // Check server state updated\n    26→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-server-counter]\")).toHaveText(\"Server Counter: 1\")\n    27→\n    28→    // Check client state received reply\n    29→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-loading]\")).toHaveText(\"Loading: false\")\n    30→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-data]\")).toContainText('\"counter\":1')\n    31→\n    32→    // Click increment by 5\n    33→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-5]\").click()\n    34→    await syncLV(page)\n    35→\n    36→    // Check server counter is now 6\n    37→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-server-counter]\")).toHaveText(\"Server Counter: 6\")\n    38→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-increment-data]\")).toContainText('\"counter\":6')\n    39→  })\n    40→\n    41→  test(\"user data fetching with different IDs\", async ({ page }) => {\n    42→    // Fetch user 1\n    43→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-fetch-user-1]\").click()\n    44→    await syncLV(page)\n    45→\n    46→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-user-loading]\")).toHaveText(\"Loading: false\")\n    47→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-user-data]\")).toContainText('\"name\":\"John Doe\"')\n    48→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-user-data]\")).toContainText('\"email\":\"john@example.com\"')\n    49→\n    50→    // Fetch user 2\n    51→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-fetch-user-2]\").click()\n    52→    await syncLV(page)\n    53→\n    54→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-user-data]\")).toContainText('\"name\":\"Jane Smith\"')\n    55→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-user-data]\")).toContainText('\"email\":\"jane@example.com\"')\n    56→\n    57→    // Fetch unknown user\n    58→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-fetch-user-999]\").click()\n    59→    await syncLV(page)\n    60→\n    61→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-user-data]\")).toContainText('\"name\":\"Unknown User\"')\n    62→  })\n    63→\n    64→  test(\"server error response handling works correctly\", async ({ page }) => {\n    65→    // Trigger server error response\n    66→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-trigger-error]\").click()\n    67→    await syncLV(page)\n    68→\n    69→    // Should receive error in data (server returns error as valid response data)\n    70→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-error-loading]\")).toHaveText(\"Loading: false\")\n    71→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-error-data]\")).toContainText('\"error\":\"Something went wrong on the server\"')\n    72→  })\n    73→\n    74→  test(\"no parameters event works\", async ({ page }) => {\n    75→    // Test ping without parameters\n    76→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-ping]\").click()\n    77→    await syncLV(page)\n    78→\n    79→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-ping-loading]\")).toHaveText(\"Loading: false\")\n    80→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-ping-data]\")).toContainText('\"response\":\"pong\"')\n    81→  })\n    82→\n    83→  test(\"different data types are handled correctly\", async ({ page }) => {\n    84→    // Test string - now wrapped in {data: \"Hello World\"}\n    85→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-test-string]\").click()\n    86→    await syncLV(page)\n    87→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-datatype-data]\")).toContainText('\"data\":\"Hello World\"')\n    88→\n    89→    // Test number - now wrapped in {data: 42}\n    90→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-test-number]\").click()\n    91→    await syncLV(page)\n    92→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-datatype-data]\")).toContainText('\"data\":42')\n    93→\n    94→    // Test boolean - now wrapped in {data: true}\n    95→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-test-boolean]\").click()\n    96→    await syncLV(page)\n    97→    await expect(page.locator(\"[data-pw-datatype-data]\")).toContainText('\"data\":true')\n    98→\n    99→    // Test array - now wrapped in {data: [1,2,3,\"four\",true]}\n   100→    await page.locator(\"[data-pw-test-array]\").click()\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2zmZWMogU2W6S6B8JQeo3","session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"d67b99be-f443-4b34-a9a8-20fd665219b2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SRAYcugjF8V87a6iUDUTu3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information needed. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of the React implementation.\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: React in LiveVite Assets\n\n### 1. Framework Renderer Interface (`renderer.ts`)\n\nThe **`FrameworkRenderer`** interface is the core abstraction that enables multi-framework support:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface FrameworkRenderer<TApp = unknown> {\n  readonly name: string\n  mount(ctx: MountContext): Promise<RendererState<TApp>> | RendererState<TApp>\n  updateProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, newProps: Record<string, any>): void\n  patchProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, operations: Operation[]): void\n  updateSlots(state: RendererState<TApp>, newSlots: Record<string, string>): void\n  unmount(state: RendererState<TApp>): void\n  renderToString?(ctx: SSRContext): Promise<string>\n}\n```\n\n**Key lifecycle:**\n- `mount()` - Creates reactive wrappers around props/slots, mounts the component\n- `updateProps()` / `patchProps()` - Updates reactive props in-place\n- `updateSlots()` - Converts slot HTML strings to framework-specific formats\n- `unmount()` - Cleans up the framework app instance\n- `renderToString()` (optional) - Server-side rendering\n\n### 2. React Renderer Implementation (`renderers/react.ts`)\n\nThe **`createReactRenderer()`** factory creates a React implementation of the `FrameworkRenderer` interface:\n\n```typescript\nexport function createReactRenderer(options: ReactRendererOptions = {}): FrameworkRenderer<ReactRendererState>\n```\n\n**Key design:**\n- Uses React 18's `createRoot` (CSR) and `hydrateRoot` (SSR)\n- Stores component, hook, and React Root instance in `ReactRendererState`\n- Props are plain mutable objects (no Vue-style reactivity needed)\n- Slots converted to React elements via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n- **Full component tree re-render on every prop/slot update** via `root.render()`\n- Wraps component in `LiveContext.Provider` so React hooks can access the LiveView hook\n\n**Slot conversion:**\n```typescript\nfunction htmlSlotsToReact(slots: Record<string, string>): Record<string, () => any> {\n  return mapValues(slots, html => () =>\n    createElement(\"span\", { dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: html.trim() } })\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**Mount flow:**\n1. Parse props and slots from DOM\n2. Create React element with `LiveContext.Provider` wrapper\n3. Call `hydrateRoot()` if SSR, else `createRoot()` and `render()`\n4. Return state with root, component, hook references\n\n### 3. Multi-Renderer Hook (`hooks.ts`)\n\nThe hook system supports both single and multi-framework setups:\n\n**`getMultiRendererHook(renderers)`** - Primary entry point:\n- Dispatches to correct renderer based on `data-framework` DOM attribute\n- Fallback: If only one renderer registered, `data-framework` is optional\n- Parses DOM attributes once (framework-agnostic)\n- Delegates framework-specific operations to selected renderer\n\n```typescript\nexport const getMultiRendererHook = (\n  renderers: Record<string, RendererEntry>\n): Hook => {\n  // Lifecycle methods:\n  // mounted() - Resolve framework, call renderer.mount()\n  // updated() - Call renderer.updateProps()/patchProps()/updateSlots()\n  // destroyed() - Call renderer.unmount()\n}\n```\n\n**`getRendererHook(renderer, resolve)`** - Convenience wrapper for single-framework:\n```typescript\nexport const getRendererHook = (renderer, resolve) =>\n  getMultiRendererHook({ [renderer.name]: { renderer, resolve } })\n```\n\n**Backward compatibility:**\n- Hook stores renderer state as `this.vue` (even for non-Vue renderers)\n- Hook stores active renderer as `this.__renderer` for use in lifecycle methods\n\n### 4. React Hooks/Composables (`useReact.ts`)\n\nCore React hooks that mirror Vue composables:\n\n#### **`useLive()`** \nReturns the LiveView hook instance from context:\n```typescript\nexport function useLive(): HookInterface {\n  return useContext(LiveContext)\n  // Provides access to pushEvent, handleEvent, liveSocket, el\n}\n```\n\n#### **`useLiveEvent(event, callback)`**\nSubscribes to LiveView server events with auto-cleanup:\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveEvent<T>(event: string, callback: (data: T) => void): void {\n  const live = useLive()\n  const callbackRef = useRef(callback)\n  \n  useEffect(() => {\n    const ref = live.handleEvent(event, (payload: T) => {\n      callbackRef.current(payload)\n    })\n    return () => live.removeHandleEvent(ref)\n  }, [live, event])\n}\n```\n\n#### **`useLiveNavigation()`**\nProvides `patch()` and `navigate()` for LiveView routing:\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveNavigation() {\n  const live = useLive()\n  \n  return {\n    patch(hrefOrQueryParams, opts?) { /* live_patch */ },\n    navigate(href, opts?) { /* live_redirect */ }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 5. React Form Hook (`useLiveFormReact.ts`)\n\nComprehensive form handling with server-side Ecto validation:\n\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveForm<T extends object>(\n  form: Form<T>,\n  options: FormOptions = {}\n): UseLiveFormReactReturn<T>\n```\n\n**Key features:**\n- Mutable form state stored in `useRef` (single \"store\" ref) to avoid stale closures\n- Version counter (`useState`) to trigger re-renders when mutable state changes\n- **Field caching** by path and options\n- **Debounced change events** (default 300ms) to server\n- **Touch tracking** (blurred fields marked as touched)\n- **Nested field access** via `field(path)` and `fieldArray(path)`\n- Array operations: `add()`, `remove()`, `move()`\n- Server updates applied to errors continuously, values only when not validating\n\n**ReactFormField interface** (mirrors Vue but without Refs):\n```typescript\nexport interface ReactFormField<T> {\n  value: T\n  errors: string[]\n  errorMessage: string | undefined\n  isValid: boolean\n  isDirty: boolean\n  isTouched: boolean\n  setValue: (newValue: T) => void\n  blur: () => void\n  inputProps: { value, onChange, onBlur, name, id, aria-invalid, ... }\n  field<K extends keyof T>(key: K): ReactFormField<T[K]>\n  fieldArray<K extends keyof T>(key: K): ReactFormFieldArray<T[K]>\n}\n```\n\n**ReactFormContext** for child components:\n- `useField(path)` - Access field from parent form context\n- `useArrayField(path)` - Access field array from parent form context\n- Must be inside `LiveFormContext.Provider`\n\n**Form state helpers:**\n```typescript\nreturn {\n  isValid, isDirty, isTouched, isValidating, submitCount, initialValues,\n  field(path), fieldArray(path),\n  submit(), reset()\n}\n```\n\n### 6. React Upload Hook (`useLiveUploadReact.ts`)\n\nFile upload integration with Phoenix LiveView:\n\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveUpload(\n  uploadConfig: UploadConfig,\n  options: UploadOptions\n): UseLiveUploadReactReturn\n```\n\n**Functionality:**\n- Creates hidden form + file input injected into LiveView element\n- Sets Phoenix LiveView upload attributes: `data-phx-hook`, `data-phx-upload-ref`, etc.\n- Updates `data-phx-*-refs` attributes as entries change\n- Tracks upload progress and validity\n\n**Return API:**\n```typescript\nexport interface UseLiveUploadReactReturn {\n  entries: UploadEntry[]\n  showFilePicker: () => void           // Click hidden input\n  addFiles: (files | DataTransfer) => void  // Add external files\n  submit: () => void                   // Dispatch form submit\n  cancel: (ref?: string) => void       // Cancel entry(ies)\n  clear: () => void                    // Reset input value\n  progress: number                     // 0-100 aggregate\n  inputEl: HTMLInputElement | null\n  valid: boolean\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Index Exports (`index.ts`)\n\nThe main library exports all React-related APIs:\n\n```typescript\n// Core hooks\nexport { useLive, useLiveEvent as useLiveEventReact, useLiveNavigation as useLiveNavigationReact, LiveContext }\n\n// Form\nexport { useLiveForm as useLiveFormReact, useField as useFieldReact, useArrayField as useArrayFieldReact, LiveFormContext }\n\n// Upload\nexport { useLiveUpload as useLiveUploadReact }\n\n// Renderer\nexport { createReactRenderer }\nexport type { FrameworkRenderer, RendererState, MountContext, SSRContext }\n```\n\n### 8. How Multi-Renderer Hook Works\n\n**Flow for React component:**\n\n1. **Elixir renders** component div with `data-framework=\"react\"` and `data-name=\"ComponentName\"`\n2. **Hook mounted()** lifecycle:\n   - Reads `data-framework=\"react\"` → selects React renderer\n   - Calls `resolve(\"ComponentName\")` → loads React component\n   - Parses `data-props`, `data-slots` from DOM\n   - Calls `renderer.mount(ctx)` → React renderer creates Root and renders\n   - Stores state in `this.vue` (backward compat) and renderer in `this.__renderer`\n\n3. **Hook updated()** lifecycle:\n   - Checks `data-use-diff=\"true\"` to decide patch vs full update\n   - Calls `renderer.updateProps()` or `renderer.patchProps()`\n   - Calls `renderer.updateSlots()` with new slot HTML\n   - React renderer calls `root.render()` to apply updates\n\n4. **Hook destroyed()** lifecycle:\n   - Calls `renderer.unmount(state)` → React renderer unmounts Root\n\n### 9. Key Design Patterns\n\n| Pattern | Details |\n|---------|---------|\n| **Props as plain objects** | React has no built-in reactivity; updates trigger explicit `root.render()` |\n| **Slots as innerHTML** | Server sends HTML strings; React renders via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| **Context for hook access** | `LiveContext` wraps component tree so hooks can call `useContext(LiveContext)` |\n| **Mutable refs for form** | Single \"store\" ref avoids stale closure issues in complex forms |\n| **Version counter trick** | `useState` counter re-renders when mutable state changes, React idiom |\n| **Caching strategies** | Form fields cached by path; array fields cached globally; reduces object creation |\n| **Event handler wrapping** | `callbackRef` in effects prevents re-runs when callback identity changes |\n| **Hidden upload form** | Upload hook injects form into LiveView element; Phoenix JS hook reads attributes |\n\n### 10. Framework-Agnostic Utilities Used\n\nFrom `utils.ts`:\n- `mapValues()` - Transform object values\n- `parsePath()` - Parse \"user.items[0].name\" to key array\n- `getValueByPath()` / `setValueByPath()` - Nested object access\n- `sanitizeId()` - Clean HTML ID from field path\n- `deepClone()` - Full object copy (uses `structuredClone` if available)\n- `deepEqual()` - Compare objects\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** The React implementation is a complete framework adapter that allows React 18+ components to work seamlessly with Phoenix LiveView, exposing the same composable APIs (form validation, uploads, events, navigation) that Vue developers use, while respecting React's render model and hooks patterns."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a79495c (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 48493\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 39363</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"7aeac3ee-6246-454a-bc11-7c3bc2a3c2e0","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the React-related files in /home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/. I need to understand:\n\n1. The React renderer implementation (look for react renderer files)\n2. The React hooks/composables (useLive, useLiveEvent, useLiveNavigation, useLiveForm, useLiveUpload)\n3. The framework renderer interface\n4. How the multi-renderer hook works\n5. How the index.ts exports React-related APIs\n\nRead all relevant files and provide a comprehensive summary.","agentId":"a79495c","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information needed. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of the React implementation.\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: React in LiveVite Assets\n\n### 1. Framework Renderer Interface (`renderer.ts`)\n\nThe **`FrameworkRenderer`** interface is the core abstraction that enables multi-framework support:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface FrameworkRenderer<TApp = unknown> {\n  readonly name: string\n  mount(ctx: MountContext): Promise<RendererState<TApp>> | RendererState<TApp>\n  updateProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, newProps: Record<string, any>): void\n  patchProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, operations: Operation[]): void\n  updateSlots(state: RendererState<TApp>, newSlots: Record<string, string>): void\n  unmount(state: RendererState<TApp>): void\n  renderToString?(ctx: SSRContext): Promise<string>\n}\n```\n\n**Key lifecycle:**\n- `mount()` - Creates reactive wrappers around props/slots, mounts the component\n- `updateProps()` / `patchProps()` - Updates reactive props in-place\n- `updateSlots()` - Converts slot HTML strings to framework-specific formats\n- `unmount()` - Cleans up the framework app instance\n- `renderToString()` (optional) - Server-side rendering\n\n### 2. React Renderer Implementation (`renderers/react.ts`)\n\nThe **`createReactRenderer()`** factory creates a React implementation of the `FrameworkRenderer` interface:\n\n```typescript\nexport function createReactRenderer(options: ReactRendererOptions = {}): FrameworkRenderer<ReactRendererState>\n```\n\n**Key design:**\n- Uses React 18's `createRoot` (CSR) and `hydrateRoot` (SSR)\n- Stores component, hook, and React Root instance in `ReactRendererState`\n- Props are plain mutable objects (no Vue-style reactivity needed)\n- Slots converted to React elements via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n- **Full component tree re-render on every prop/slot update** via `root.render()`\n- Wraps component in `LiveContext.Provider` so React hooks can access the LiveView hook\n\n**Slot conversion:**\n```typescript\nfunction htmlSlotsToReact(slots: Record<string, string>): Record<string, () => any> {\n  return mapValues(slots, html => () =>\n    createElement(\"span\", { dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: html.trim() } })\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**Mount flow:**\n1. Parse props and slots from DOM\n2. Create React element with `LiveContext.Provider` wrapper\n3. Call `hydrateRoot()` if SSR, else `createRoot()` and `render()`\n4. Return state with root, component, hook references\n\n### 3. Multi-Renderer Hook (`hooks.ts`)\n\nThe hook system supports both single and multi-framework setups:\n\n**`getMultiRendererHook(renderers)`** - Primary entry point:\n- Dispatches to correct renderer based on `data-framework` DOM attribute\n- Fallback: If only one renderer registered, `data-framework` is optional\n- Parses DOM attributes once (framework-agnostic)\n- Delegates framework-specific operations to selected renderer\n\n```typescript\nexport const getMultiRendererHook = (\n  renderers: Record<string, RendererEntry>\n): Hook => {\n  // Lifecycle methods:\n  // mounted() - Resolve framework, call renderer.mount()\n  // updated() - Call renderer.updateProps()/patchProps()/updateSlots()\n  // destroyed() - Call renderer.unmount()\n}\n```\n\n**`getRendererHook(renderer, resolve)`** - Convenience wrapper for single-framework:\n```typescript\nexport const getRendererHook = (renderer, resolve) =>\n  getMultiRendererHook({ [renderer.name]: { renderer, resolve } })\n```\n\n**Backward compatibility:**\n- Hook stores renderer state as `this.vue` (even for non-Vue renderers)\n- Hook stores active renderer as `this.__renderer` for use in lifecycle methods\n\n### 4. React Hooks/Composables (`useReact.ts`)\n\nCore React hooks that mirror Vue composables:\n\n#### **`useLive()`** \nReturns the LiveView hook instance from context:\n```typescript\nexport function useLive(): HookInterface {\n  return useContext(LiveContext)\n  // Provides access to pushEvent, handleEvent, liveSocket, el\n}\n```\n\n#### **`useLiveEvent(event, callback)`**\nSubscribes to LiveView server events with auto-cleanup:\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveEvent<T>(event: string, callback: (data: T) => void): void {\n  const live = useLive()\n  const callbackRef = useRef(callback)\n  \n  useEffect(() => {\n    const ref = live.handleEvent(event, (payload: T) => {\n      callbackRef.current(payload)\n    })\n    return () => live.removeHandleEvent(ref)\n  }, [live, event])\n}\n```\n\n#### **`useLiveNavigation()`**\nProvides `patch()` and `navigate()` for LiveView routing:\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveNavigation() {\n  const live = useLive()\n  \n  return {\n    patch(hrefOrQueryParams, opts?) { /* live_patch */ },\n    navigate(href, opts?) { /* live_redirect */ }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 5. React Form Hook (`useLiveFormReact.ts`)\n\nComprehensive form handling with server-side Ecto validation:\n\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveForm<T extends object>(\n  form: Form<T>,\n  options: FormOptions = {}\n): UseLiveFormReactReturn<T>\n```\n\n**Key features:**\n- Mutable form state stored in `useRef` (single \"store\" ref) to avoid stale closures\n- Version counter (`useState`) to trigger re-renders when mutable state changes\n- **Field caching** by path and options\n- **Debounced change events** (default 300ms) to server\n- **Touch tracking** (blurred fields marked as touched)\n- **Nested field access** via `field(path)` and `fieldArray(path)`\n- Array operations: `add()`, `remove()`, `move()`\n- Server updates applied to errors continuously, values only when not validating\n\n**ReactFormField interface** (mirrors Vue but without Refs):\n```typescript\nexport interface ReactFormField<T> {\n  value: T\n  errors: string[]\n  errorMessage: string | undefined\n  isValid: boolean\n  isDirty: boolean\n  isTouched: boolean\n  setValue: (newValue: T) => void\n  blur: () => void\n  inputProps: { value, onChange, onBlur, name, id, aria-invalid, ... }\n  field<K extends keyof T>(key: K): ReactFormField<T[K]>\n  fieldArray<K extends keyof T>(key: K): ReactFormFieldArray<T[K]>\n}\n```\n\n**ReactFormContext** for child components:\n- `useField(path)` - Access field from parent form context\n- `useArrayField(path)` - Access field array from parent form context\n- Must be inside `LiveFormContext.Provider`\n\n**Form state helpers:**\n```typescript\nreturn {\n  isValid, isDirty, isTouched, isValidating, submitCount, initialValues,\n  field(path), fieldArray(path),\n  submit(), reset()\n}\n```\n\n### 6. React Upload Hook (`useLiveUploadReact.ts`)\n\nFile upload integration with Phoenix LiveView:\n\n```typescript\nexport function useLiveUpload(\n  uploadConfig: UploadConfig,\n  options: UploadOptions\n): UseLiveUploadReactReturn\n```\n\n**Functionality:**\n- Creates hidden form + file input injected into LiveView element\n- Sets Phoenix LiveView upload attributes: `data-phx-hook`, `data-phx-upload-ref`, etc.\n- Updates `data-phx-*-refs` attributes as entries change\n- Tracks upload progress and validity\n\n**Return API:**\n```typescript\nexport interface UseLiveUploadReactReturn {\n  entries: UploadEntry[]\n  showFilePicker: () => void           // Click hidden input\n  addFiles: (files | DataTransfer) => void  // Add external files\n  submit: () => void                   // Dispatch form submit\n  cancel: (ref?: string) => void       // Cancel entry(ies)\n  clear: () => void                    // Reset input value\n  progress: number                     // 0-100 aggregate\n  inputEl: HTMLInputElement | null\n  valid: boolean\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Index Exports (`index.ts`)\n\nThe main library exports all React-related APIs:\n\n```typescript\n// Core hooks\nexport { useLive, useLiveEvent as useLiveEventReact, useLiveNavigation as useLiveNavigationReact, LiveContext }\n\n// Form\nexport { useLiveForm as useLiveFormReact, useField as useFieldReact, useArrayField as useArrayFieldReact, LiveFormContext }\n\n// Upload\nexport { useLiveUpload as useLiveUploadReact }\n\n// Renderer\nexport { createReactRenderer }\nexport type { FrameworkRenderer, RendererState, MountContext, SSRContext }\n```\n\n### 8. How Multi-Renderer Hook Works\n\n**Flow for React component:**\n\n1. **Elixir renders** component div with `data-framework=\"react\"` and `data-name=\"ComponentName\"`\n2. **Hook mounted()** lifecycle:\n   - Reads `data-framework=\"react\"` → selects React renderer\n   - Calls `resolve(\"ComponentName\")` → loads React component\n   - Parses `data-props`, `data-slots` from DOM\n   - Calls `renderer.mount(ctx)` → React renderer creates Root and renders\n   - Stores state in `this.vue` (backward compat) and renderer in `this.__renderer`\n\n3. **Hook updated()** lifecycle:\n   - Checks `data-use-diff=\"true\"` to decide patch vs full update\n   - Calls `renderer.updateProps()` or `renderer.patchProps()`\n   - Calls `renderer.updateSlots()` with new slot HTML\n   - React renderer calls `root.render()` to apply updates\n\n4. **Hook destroyed()** lifecycle:\n   - Calls `renderer.unmount(state)` → React renderer unmounts Root\n\n### 9. Key Design Patterns\n\n| Pattern | Details |\n|---------|---------|\n| **Props as plain objects** | React has no built-in reactivity; updates trigger explicit `root.render()` |\n| **Slots as innerHTML** | Server sends HTML strings; React renders via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| **Context for hook access** | `LiveContext` wraps component tree so hooks can call `useContext(LiveContext)` |\n| **Mutable refs for form** | Single \"store\" ref avoids stale closure issues in complex forms |\n| **Version counter trick** | `useState` counter re-renders when mutable state changes, React idiom |\n| **Caching strategies** | Form fields cached by path; array fields cached globally; reduces object creation |\n| **Event handler wrapping** | `callbackRef` in effects prevents re-runs when callback identity changes |\n| **Hidden upload form** | Upload hook injects form into LiveView element; Phoenix JS hook reads attributes |\n\n### 10. Framework-Agnostic Utilities Used\n\nFrom `utils.ts`:\n- `mapValues()` - Transform object values\n- `parsePath()` - Parse \"user.items[0].name\" to key array\n- `getValueByPath()` / `setValueByPath()` - Nested object access\n- `sanitizeId()` - Clean HTML ID from field path\n- `deepClone()` - Full object copy (uses `structuredClone` if available)\n- `deepEqual()` - Compare objects\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** The React implementation is a complete framework adapter that allows React 18+ components to work seamlessly with Phoenix LiveView, exposing the same composable APIs (form validation, uploads, events, navigation) that Vue developers use, while respecting React's render model and hooks patterns."}],"totalDurationMs":39363,"totalTokens":48493,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2296,"cache_read_input_tokens":43217,"output_tokens":2974,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2296,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2zmZWMogU2W6S6B8JQeo3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a detailed summary report.\n\n## Comprehensive E2E Test Structure Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the E2E test structure in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/`. Here's a detailed breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERALL DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\ntest/e2e/\n├── playwright.config.js       # Playwright configuration\n├── utils.js                   # Test utilities (syncLV, evalLV, randomString)\n├── vite.config.js             # Vite build config for test assets\n├── js/app.js                  # Vue + LiveView initialization\n├── test_helper.exs            # Elixir test server setup & router\n├── priv/static/               # Built test assets (output)\n└── features/                  # Feature test suites (11 features)\n    ├── basic/                 # Counter component\n    ├── dead-view/             # Controller-based rendering\n    ├── event/                 # useLiveEvent hook\n    ├── event-reply/           # Event reply patterns\n    ├── form/                  # useLiveForm with Ecto validation\n    ├── memory-benchmark/      # Performance testing\n    ├── navigation/            # useLiveNavigation\n    ├── prop-diff/             # JSON Patch diffing\n    ├── slot/                  # Slot rendering\n    ├── stream/                # LiveView Streams\n    └── upload/                # useLiveUpload hook\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. FEATURE ORGANIZATION PATTERN\n\nEach feature directory follows a **colocated structure** with three core files:\n\n### **live.ex** (Elixir LiveView Module)\n- Phoenix LiveView module handling server logic\n- Defines socket initialization, event handlers, state\n- Uses `~H\"\"\"` HEX templates to render the Vue component\n- Example: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/features/basic/live.ex`\n  ```elixir\n  defmodule LiveVite.E2E.TestLive do\n    use Phoenix.LiveView\n    \n    def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n      {:ok, assign(socket, :counter, 0)}\n    end\n    \n    def handle_event(\"increment\", %{\"value\" => value}, socket) do\n      {:noreply, assign(socket, :counter, socket.assigns.counter + value)}\n    end\n    \n    def render(assigns) do\n      ~H\"\"\"\n      <LiveVite.vue count={@counter} v-component=\"counter\" v-socket={@socket} />\n      \"\"\"\n    end\n  end\n  ```\n\n### **\\*.vue** (Vue Components)\n- Single-file Vue 3 components with `<script setup>` syntax\n- Use TypeScript by default\n- Import LiveVite composables (`useLiveVite`, `useLiveEvent`, `useLiveForm`, `useLiveUpload`, `useLiveNavigation`)\n- Use `$live.pushEvent()` to send events to server\n- Use data attributes (`data-pw-*`) for test selectors\n- Example: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/features/basic/counter.vue`\n  ```vue\n  <script setup lang=\"ts\">\n  import { ref } from \"vue\"\n  const props = defineProps<{ count: number }>()\n  const diff = ref<number>(1)\n  </script>\n  \n  <template>\n    Current count: <div data-pw-counter>{{ props.count }}</div>\n    <input v-model.number=\"diff\" type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"10\" />\n    <button @click=\"$live.pushEvent('increment', { value: diff })\">\n      Increase by {{ diff }}\n    </button>\n  </template>\n  ```\n\n### **\\*.spec.js** (Playwright Tests)\n- Playwright test files following standard test structure\n- Use `test.describe()` for grouping, `test()` for individual tests\n- Use `syncLV(page)` utility to wait for LiveView to be ready\n- Use `evalLV(page, code)` to evaluate Elixir code in the server context\n- Common patterns:\n  - `page.goto(url)` → `syncLV(page)` → assertions\n  - Interact with page → `syncLV()` → verify updates\n  - Data attributes for selectors: `page.locator('[data-pw-*]')`\n\n---\n\n## 3. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/playwright.config.js`\n\n```javascript\n{\n  testDir: \"./features\",           // Test files auto-discovered\n  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,   // Fail if .only() used in CI\n  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,\n  expect: { timeout: 1000 },\n  use: {\n    trace: \"retain-on-failure\",   // Debug traces on failure\n    screenshot: \"only-on-failure\",\n    baseURL: \"http://localhost:4004/\",\n  },\n  webServer: {\n    command: \"cd ../.. && MIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs\",\n    url: \"http://127.0.0.1:4004/health\",\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 60_000,\n  },\n  projects: [\n    { name: \"chromium\", use: { ...devices[\"Desktop Chrome\"] } },\n    // Firefox and Safari commented out\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Auto-starts Elixir test server** via webServer\n- **Single Chromium browser** for CI/local\n- **Health check endpoint** (`/health`) for ready detection\n- **Reuses server** in local dev, restarts in CI\n\n---\n\n## 4. TEST UTILITIES\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/utils.js`\n\n### **syncLV(page)**\nWaits for LiveView to be ready before continuing:\n```javascript\nconst syncLV = async page => {\n  const connectionTimeout = { timeout: 5000 }\n  const promises = [\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-connected\").first()).toBeVisible(connectionTimeout),\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-change-loading\")).toHaveCount(0),\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-click-loading\")).toHaveCount(0),\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-submit-loading\")).toHaveCount(0),\n    new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 50)),\n  ]\n  return Promise.all(promises)\n}\n```\n- Waits for WebSocket connection (`.phx-connected`)\n- Waits for all pending events to clear (no `.phx-*-loading` classes)\n- Adds 50ms buffer for Vue reactivity\n\n### **evalLV(page, code, selector?)**\nExecutes Elixir code in the LiveView process context:\n```javascript\nconst evalLV = async (page, code, selector = \"[data-phx-main]\") =>\n  await page.evaluate(([code, selector]) => {\n    return new Promise(resolve => {\n      window.liveSocket.main.withinTargets(selector, (targetView, targetCtx) => {\n        targetView.pushEvent(\n          \"event\",\n          document.body,\n          targetCtx,\n          \"sandbox:eval\",\n          { value: code },\n          {},\n          ({ result, error }) => { /* handle result */ }\n        )\n      })\n    })\n  }, [code, selector])\n```\n- Sends code to server as `\"sandbox:eval\"` event\n- Waits for response asynchronously\n- Used for advanced assertions or debugging\n\n### **randomString(length)**\nGenerates random alphanumeric strings for test isolation\n\n---\n\n## 5. ELIXIR TEST SERVER SETUP\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/test_helper.exs`\n\n### **Core Components:**\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Endpoint** (Phoenix Endpoint)\n- Runs on `http://127.0.0.1:4004`\n- Serves Vite-built assets from `test/e2e/priv/static/assets`\n- Includes Phoenix and LiveView static assets\n- Health check endpoint at `/health`\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Router** (Phoenix Router)\n```elixir\nlive_session :default, layout: {Layout, :live}, on_mount: {LiveVite.E2E.Hooks, :default} do\n  scope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E do\n    pipe_through(:browser)\n    live \"/test\", TestLive                          # Basic counter\n    live \"/prop-diff-test\", PropDiffTestLive\n    live \"/navigation/:page\", NavigationLive\n    live \"/navigation/alt/:page\", NavigationLive\n    live \"/events\", EventLive\n    live \"/upload/:mode\", UploadTestLive\n    live \"/streams\", StreamLive\n    live \"/form-test\", FormTestLive\n    live \"/event-reply-test\", EventReplyTestLive\n    live \"/slot-test\", SlotTestLive\n    live \"/memory-benchmark\", MemoryBenchmarkLive\n  end\nend\n\n# Dead view route (non-LiveView)\nscope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E do\n  pipe_through(:browser)\n  get \"/dead-view\", DeadViewController, :show\nend\n```\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Hooks** (on_mount hook)\n- Provides `\"sandbox:eval\"` event handler\n- Allows tests to execute Elixir code: `Code.eval_string(code, [socket: socket], __ENV__)`\n- Returns result via event reply\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Layout** (HEX templates)\n- Root layout: Basic HTML structure with meta tags\n- Live layout: Includes Vite-built `app.js` and `app.css`\n\n---\n\n## 6. VUE/JAVASCRIPT INITIALIZATION\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/js/app.js`\n\n```javascript\nimport { getHooks, createLiveVite, findComponent } from \"live_vite\"\n\nconst liveViteApp = createLiveVite({\n  resolve: name => {\n    const components = {\n      ...import.meta.glob(\"../features/**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n    }\n    return findComponent(components, name)\n  },\n  setup: ({ createApp, component, props, slots, plugin, el }) => {\n    const app = createApp({ render: () => h(component, props, slots) })\n    app.use(plugin)\n    app.mount(el)\n    return app\n  },\n})\n\nlet liveSocket = new LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n  params: { _csrf_token: csrfToken },\n  hooks: getHooks(liveViteApp),\n})\n\nliveSocket.connect()\nwindow.liveSocket = liveSocket  // Exposed for tests\n```\n\n**Key Pattern:**\n- Uses glob to auto-discover all `.vue` files in features\n- `getHooks()` returns Phoenix LiveView hooks for Vue integration\n- `window.liveSocket` accessible to test utils for `evalLV()`\n\n---\n\n## 7. VITE BUILD CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/vite.config.js`\n\n```javascript\nexport default defineConfig(({ command }) => {\n  return {\n    base: \"/assets\",\n    plugins: [vue()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        vue: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../node_modules/vue\"),\n        \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\"),\n        live_vite: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../assets/index.ts\"),\n      },\n    },\n    build: {\n      commonjsOptions: { transformMixedEsModules: true },\n      target: \"es2020\",\n      outDir: \"./test/e2e/priv/static/assets\",\n      emptyOutDir: true,\n      rollupOptions: {\n        input: { app: path.resolve(__dirname, \"./js/app.js\") },\n        output: {\n          entryFileNames: \"[name].js\",      // app.js (no hash)\n          chunkFileNames: \"[name].js\",\n          assetFileNames: \"[name][extname]\",\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  }\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. TEST PATTERNS & CONVENTIONS\n\n### **File Naming:**\n- Components: `ComponentName.vue` (PascalCase)\n- Specs: `feature-name.spec.js` (kebab-case)\n- LiveView modules: `FeatureNameLive` (same as routes)\n- Test data attributes: `data-pw-*` (playwright markers)\n\n### **Test Structure Pattern:**\n```javascript\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\"\nimport { syncLV } from \"../../utils.js\"\n\ntest.describe(\"Feature Description\", () => {\n  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n    await page.goto(\"/route\")\n    await syncLV(page)\n  })\n\n  test(\"should do something\", async ({ page }) => {\n    // Arrange: element selection\n    const element = page.locator('[data-pw-selector]')\n    \n    // Act: user interaction\n    await element.click()\n    await syncLV(page)\n    \n    // Assert: verify outcome\n    await expect(element).toHaveText(\"expected\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n### **Common Assertions:**\n- `.toBeVisible()` - Element exists and visible\n- `.toHaveText(text)` - Exact text match\n- `.toContainText(text)` - Partial text match\n- `.toHaveValue(value)` - Input field value\n- `.toHaveCount(n)` - Number of matching elements\n- `.toHaveAttribute(name, value)` - HTML attribute\n- `.toBeDisabled()` / `.toBeEnabled()` - Button state\n- `.toBeChecked()` / `.not.toBeChecked()` - Checkbox state\n\n### **Event Patterns:**\n```javascript\n// Push event from Vue to server\nawait page.click('[data-pw-button]')  // Vue button with @click=\"$live.pushEvent(...)\"\nawait syncLV(page)\n\n// Form input changes (auto-send via change/blur)\nawait page.fill('[data-pw-input]', \"value\")\nawait syncLV(page)\n\n// File uploads\nawait page.setInputFiles('input[type=\"file\"]', { name: \"file.txt\", ... })\nawait syncLV(page)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. FEATURE BREAKDOWN\n\n| Feature | Purpose | Key Composables | Test Files |\n|---------|---------|-----------------|-----------|\n| **basic** | Counter increments | `useLiveVite()` | 1 spec |\n| **dead-view** | Non-LiveView Phoenix controller | Via `~VUE` sigil | 1 spec |\n| **event** | Server → Client events | `useLiveEvent()` | 1 spec, 4 tests |\n| **event-reply** | Client → Server with replies | `useLiveVite()` | 1 spec, 20+ tests |\n| **form** | Ecto validation & state | `useLiveForm()` | 1 spec, 13 tests |\n| **memory-benchmark** | Performance testing | All composables | No spec (manual) |\n| **navigation** | Route patching/navigation | `useLiveNavigation()` | 1 spec, 2 tests |\n| **prop-diff** | JSON Patch efficiency | None (server-side) | 1 spec, 15 tests |\n| **slot** | Non-ASCII slot content | Vue slots | 1 spec, 5 tests |\n| **stream** | LiveView Streams | `useLiveVite()` | 1 spec, 15 tests |\n| **upload** | File uploads | `useLiveUpload()` | 1 spec, 11 tests |\n\n---\n\n## 10. KEY TESTING PATTERNS\n\n### **Pattern: Props Diffing Verification**\n```javascript\nconst getProps = async page => {\n  await syncLV(page)\n  const propsJson = await page.locator('[data-testid=\"props-json\"]').textContent()\n  return JSON.parse(propsJson)\n}\n\ntest(\"changes applied via diff\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.locator('[data-testid=\"btn-change\"]').click()\n  const props = await getProps(page)\n  expect(props.value).toBe(\"new\")\n})\n```\n\n### **Pattern: Form Validation**\n```javascript\ntest(\"validation errors appear\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.locator('[data-pw-input]').fill(\"invalid\")\n  await page.locator('[data-pw-input]').blur()\n  await syncLV(page)\n  \n  await expect(page.locator('[data-pw-error]')).toBeVisible()\n  await expect(page.locator('[data-pw-is-valid]')).toHaveText(\"Valid: false\")\n})\n```\n\n### **Pattern: Stream Operations**\n```javascript\ntest(\"adds item to stream\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.fill('[data-testid=\"name-input\"]', \"New Item\")\n  await page.click('[data-testid=\"add-button\"]')\n  await syncLV(page)\n  \n  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid=\"item-4\"]')).toBeVisible()\n  const heading = page.locator('h3:has-text(\"Items\")')\n  await expect(heading).toHaveText(\"Items (4)\")\n})\n```\n\n### **Pattern: Event Reply (Request/Response)**\n```javascript\ntest(\"event reply data received\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.locator('[data-pw-fetch-user-1]').click()\n  await syncLV(page)\n  \n  await expect(page.locator('[data-pw-user-data]')).toContainText('\"name\":\"John\"')\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. CONFIGURATION & CONVENTIONS\n\n**In mix.exs:**\n- `elixirc_paths: [..., \"test/e2e/features/*/\"]` - Compiles all feature LiveView modules\n\n**Environment:**\n```bash\nMIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs  # Starts server\nnpm run e2e:test                              # Runs tests against server\n```\n\n**Browser Testing:**\n- Only Chromium enabled (Firefox/Safari commented out)\n- Traces & screenshots on failure\n- Health check at `http://localhost:4004/health`\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe E2E test structure is **feature-centric and colocated**, with each feature containing:\n1. **LiveView module** (`live.ex`) - Server logic\n2. **Vue component(s)** (`.vue`) - Client UI\n3. **Playwright spec** (`.spec.js`) - Test scenarios\n4. **Optional controller** (for dead view patterns)\n\nTests follow **arrange-act-assert** with **syncLV() synchronization** between page interactions and assertions. The setup leverages Vite for component bundling, Phoenix for routing/state, and Playwright for automation—all coordinated through a shared `window.liveSocket` reference."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: adaa09a (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 64620\ntool_uses: 24\nduration_ms: 64032</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"f772a2f8-9c5e-45b8-a098-e11fbbe8045e","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the E2E test structure in /home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/. I need to understand:\n\n1. All feature directories and their contents (live.ex, vue components, spec files)\n2. The test_helper.exs router setup\n3. The utils.js helpers\n4. The playwright config\n5. How tests are structured (imports, test patterns, assertions)\n\nRead all the key files and provide a comprehensive summary of the patterns used.","agentId":"adaa09a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a detailed summary report.\n\n## Comprehensive E2E Test Structure Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the E2E test structure in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/`. Here's a detailed breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERALL DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\ntest/e2e/\n├── playwright.config.js       # Playwright configuration\n├── utils.js                   # Test utilities (syncLV, evalLV, randomString)\n├── vite.config.js             # Vite build config for test assets\n├── js/app.js                  # Vue + LiveView initialization\n├── test_helper.exs            # Elixir test server setup & router\n├── priv/static/               # Built test assets (output)\n└── features/                  # Feature test suites (11 features)\n    ├── basic/                 # Counter component\n    ├── dead-view/             # Controller-based rendering\n    ├── event/                 # useLiveEvent hook\n    ├── event-reply/           # Event reply patterns\n    ├── form/                  # useLiveForm with Ecto validation\n    ├── memory-benchmark/      # Performance testing\n    ├── navigation/            # useLiveNavigation\n    ├── prop-diff/             # JSON Patch diffing\n    ├── slot/                  # Slot rendering\n    ├── stream/                # LiveView Streams\n    └── upload/                # useLiveUpload hook\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. FEATURE ORGANIZATION PATTERN\n\nEach feature directory follows a **colocated structure** with three core files:\n\n### **live.ex** (Elixir LiveView Module)\n- Phoenix LiveView module handling server logic\n- Defines socket initialization, event handlers, state\n- Uses `~H\"\"\"` HEX templates to render the Vue component\n- Example: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/features/basic/live.ex`\n  ```elixir\n  defmodule LiveVite.E2E.TestLive do\n    use Phoenix.LiveView\n    \n    def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n      {:ok, assign(socket, :counter, 0)}\n    end\n    \n    def handle_event(\"increment\", %{\"value\" => value}, socket) do\n      {:noreply, assign(socket, :counter, socket.assigns.counter + value)}\n    end\n    \n    def render(assigns) do\n      ~H\"\"\"\n      <LiveVite.vue count={@counter} v-component=\"counter\" v-socket={@socket} />\n      \"\"\"\n    end\n  end\n  ```\n\n### **\\*.vue** (Vue Components)\n- Single-file Vue 3 components with `<script setup>` syntax\n- Use TypeScript by default\n- Import LiveVite composables (`useLiveVite`, `useLiveEvent`, `useLiveForm`, `useLiveUpload`, `useLiveNavigation`)\n- Use `$live.pushEvent()` to send events to server\n- Use data attributes (`data-pw-*`) for test selectors\n- Example: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/features/basic/counter.vue`\n  ```vue\n  <script setup lang=\"ts\">\n  import { ref } from \"vue\"\n  const props = defineProps<{ count: number }>()\n  const diff = ref<number>(1)\n  </script>\n  \n  <template>\n    Current count: <div data-pw-counter>{{ props.count }}</div>\n    <input v-model.number=\"diff\" type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"10\" />\n    <button @click=\"$live.pushEvent('increment', { value: diff })\">\n      Increase by {{ diff }}\n    </button>\n  </template>\n  ```\n\n### **\\*.spec.js** (Playwright Tests)\n- Playwright test files following standard test structure\n- Use `test.describe()` for grouping, `test()` for individual tests\n- Use `syncLV(page)` utility to wait for LiveView to be ready\n- Use `evalLV(page, code)` to evaluate Elixir code in the server context\n- Common patterns:\n  - `page.goto(url)` → `syncLV(page)` → assertions\n  - Interact with page → `syncLV()` → verify updates\n  - Data attributes for selectors: `page.locator('[data-pw-*]')`\n\n---\n\n## 3. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/playwright.config.js`\n\n```javascript\n{\n  testDir: \"./features\",           // Test files auto-discovered\n  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,   // Fail if .only() used in CI\n  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,\n  expect: { timeout: 1000 },\n  use: {\n    trace: \"retain-on-failure\",   // Debug traces on failure\n    screenshot: \"only-on-failure\",\n    baseURL: \"http://localhost:4004/\",\n  },\n  webServer: {\n    command: \"cd ../.. && MIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs\",\n    url: \"http://127.0.0.1:4004/health\",\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 60_000,\n  },\n  projects: [\n    { name: \"chromium\", use: { ...devices[\"Desktop Chrome\"] } },\n    // Firefox and Safari commented out\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Auto-starts Elixir test server** via webServer\n- **Single Chromium browser** for CI/local\n- **Health check endpoint** (`/health`) for ready detection\n- **Reuses server** in local dev, restarts in CI\n\n---\n\n## 4. TEST UTILITIES\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/utils.js`\n\n### **syncLV(page)**\nWaits for LiveView to be ready before continuing:\n```javascript\nconst syncLV = async page => {\n  const connectionTimeout = { timeout: 5000 }\n  const promises = [\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-connected\").first()).toBeVisible(connectionTimeout),\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-change-loading\")).toHaveCount(0),\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-click-loading\")).toHaveCount(0),\n    expect(page.locator(\".phx-submit-loading\")).toHaveCount(0),\n    new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 50)),\n  ]\n  return Promise.all(promises)\n}\n```\n- Waits for WebSocket connection (`.phx-connected`)\n- Waits for all pending events to clear (no `.phx-*-loading` classes)\n- Adds 50ms buffer for Vue reactivity\n\n### **evalLV(page, code, selector?)**\nExecutes Elixir code in the LiveView process context:\n```javascript\nconst evalLV = async (page, code, selector = \"[data-phx-main]\") =>\n  await page.evaluate(([code, selector]) => {\n    return new Promise(resolve => {\n      window.liveSocket.main.withinTargets(selector, (targetView, targetCtx) => {\n        targetView.pushEvent(\n          \"event\",\n          document.body,\n          targetCtx,\n          \"sandbox:eval\",\n          { value: code },\n          {},\n          ({ result, error }) => { /* handle result */ }\n        )\n      })\n    })\n  }, [code, selector])\n```\n- Sends code to server as `\"sandbox:eval\"` event\n- Waits for response asynchronously\n- Used for advanced assertions or debugging\n\n### **randomString(length)**\nGenerates random alphanumeric strings for test isolation\n\n---\n\n## 5. ELIXIR TEST SERVER SETUP\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/test_helper.exs`\n\n### **Core Components:**\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Endpoint** (Phoenix Endpoint)\n- Runs on `http://127.0.0.1:4004`\n- Serves Vite-built assets from `test/e2e/priv/static/assets`\n- Includes Phoenix and LiveView static assets\n- Health check endpoint at `/health`\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Router** (Phoenix Router)\n```elixir\nlive_session :default, layout: {Layout, :live}, on_mount: {LiveVite.E2E.Hooks, :default} do\n  scope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E do\n    pipe_through(:browser)\n    live \"/test\", TestLive                          # Basic counter\n    live \"/prop-diff-test\", PropDiffTestLive\n    live \"/navigation/:page\", NavigationLive\n    live \"/navigation/alt/:page\", NavigationLive\n    live \"/events\", EventLive\n    live \"/upload/:mode\", UploadTestLive\n    live \"/streams\", StreamLive\n    live \"/form-test\", FormTestLive\n    live \"/event-reply-test\", EventReplyTestLive\n    live \"/slot-test\", SlotTestLive\n    live \"/memory-benchmark\", MemoryBenchmarkLive\n  end\nend\n\n# Dead view route (non-LiveView)\nscope \"/\", LiveVite.E2E do\n  pipe_through(:browser)\n  get \"/dead-view\", DeadViewController, :show\nend\n```\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Hooks** (on_mount hook)\n- Provides `\"sandbox:eval\"` event handler\n- Allows tests to execute Elixir code: `Code.eval_string(code, [socket: socket], __ENV__)`\n- Returns result via event reply\n\n**LiveVite.E2E.Layout** (HEX templates)\n- Root layout: Basic HTML structure with meta tags\n- Live layout: Includes Vite-built `app.js` and `app.css`\n\n---\n\n## 6. VUE/JAVASCRIPT INITIALIZATION\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/js/app.js`\n\n```javascript\nimport { getHooks, createLiveVite, findComponent } from \"live_vite\"\n\nconst liveViteApp = createLiveVite({\n  resolve: name => {\n    const components = {\n      ...import.meta.glob(\"../features/**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n    }\n    return findComponent(components, name)\n  },\n  setup: ({ createApp, component, props, slots, plugin, el }) => {\n    const app = createApp({ render: () => h(component, props, slots) })\n    app.use(plugin)\n    app.mount(el)\n    return app\n  },\n})\n\nlet liveSocket = new LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n  params: { _csrf_token: csrfToken },\n  hooks: getHooks(liveViteApp),\n})\n\nliveSocket.connect()\nwindow.liveSocket = liveSocket  // Exposed for tests\n```\n\n**Key Pattern:**\n- Uses glob to auto-discover all `.vue` files in features\n- `getHooks()` returns Phoenix LiveView hooks for Vue integration\n- `window.liveSocket` accessible to test utils for `evalLV()`\n\n---\n\n## 7. VITE BUILD CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/vite.config.js`\n\n```javascript\nexport default defineConfig(({ command }) => {\n  return {\n    base: \"/assets\",\n    plugins: [vue()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        vue: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../node_modules/vue\"),\n        \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\"),\n        live_vite: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../assets/index.ts\"),\n      },\n    },\n    build: {\n      commonjsOptions: { transformMixedEsModules: true },\n      target: \"es2020\",\n      outDir: \"./test/e2e/priv/static/assets\",\n      emptyOutDir: true,\n      rollupOptions: {\n        input: { app: path.resolve(__dirname, \"./js/app.js\") },\n        output: {\n          entryFileNames: \"[name].js\",      // app.js (no hash)\n          chunkFileNames: \"[name].js\",\n          assetFileNames: \"[name][extname]\",\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  }\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. TEST PATTERNS & CONVENTIONS\n\n### **File Naming:**\n- Components: `ComponentName.vue` (PascalCase)\n- Specs: `feature-name.spec.js` (kebab-case)\n- LiveView modules: `FeatureNameLive` (same as routes)\n- Test data attributes: `data-pw-*` (playwright markers)\n\n### **Test Structure Pattern:**\n```javascript\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\"\nimport { syncLV } from \"../../utils.js\"\n\ntest.describe(\"Feature Description\", () => {\n  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n    await page.goto(\"/route\")\n    await syncLV(page)\n  })\n\n  test(\"should do something\", async ({ page }) => {\n    // Arrange: element selection\n    const element = page.locator('[data-pw-selector]')\n    \n    // Act: user interaction\n    await element.click()\n    await syncLV(page)\n    \n    // Assert: verify outcome\n    await expect(element).toHaveText(\"expected\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n### **Common Assertions:**\n- `.toBeVisible()` - Element exists and visible\n- `.toHaveText(text)` - Exact text match\n- `.toContainText(text)` - Partial text match\n- `.toHaveValue(value)` - Input field value\n- `.toHaveCount(n)` - Number of matching elements\n- `.toHaveAttribute(name, value)` - HTML attribute\n- `.toBeDisabled()` / `.toBeEnabled()` - Button state\n- `.toBeChecked()` / `.not.toBeChecked()` - Checkbox state\n\n### **Event Patterns:**\n```javascript\n// Push event from Vue to server\nawait page.click('[data-pw-button]')  // Vue button with @click=\"$live.pushEvent(...)\"\nawait syncLV(page)\n\n// Form input changes (auto-send via change/blur)\nawait page.fill('[data-pw-input]', \"value\")\nawait syncLV(page)\n\n// File uploads\nawait page.setInputFiles('input[type=\"file\"]', { name: \"file.txt\", ... })\nawait syncLV(page)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. FEATURE BREAKDOWN\n\n| Feature | Purpose | Key Composables | Test Files |\n|---------|---------|-----------------|-----------|\n| **basic** | Counter increments | `useLiveVite()` | 1 spec |\n| **dead-view** | Non-LiveView Phoenix controller | Via `~VUE` sigil | 1 spec |\n| **event** | Server → Client events | `useLiveEvent()` | 1 spec, 4 tests |\n| **event-reply** | Client → Server with replies | `useLiveVite()` | 1 spec, 20+ tests |\n| **form** | Ecto validation & state | `useLiveForm()` | 1 spec, 13 tests |\n| **memory-benchmark** | Performance testing | All composables | No spec (manual) |\n| **navigation** | Route patching/navigation | `useLiveNavigation()` | 1 spec, 2 tests |\n| **prop-diff** | JSON Patch efficiency | None (server-side) | 1 spec, 15 tests |\n| **slot** | Non-ASCII slot content | Vue slots | 1 spec, 5 tests |\n| **stream** | LiveView Streams | `useLiveVite()` | 1 spec, 15 tests |\n| **upload** | File uploads | `useLiveUpload()` | 1 spec, 11 tests |\n\n---\n\n## 10. KEY TESTING PATTERNS\n\n### **Pattern: Props Diffing Verification**\n```javascript\nconst getProps = async page => {\n  await syncLV(page)\n  const propsJson = await page.locator('[data-testid=\"props-json\"]').textContent()\n  return JSON.parse(propsJson)\n}\n\ntest(\"changes applied via diff\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.locator('[data-testid=\"btn-change\"]').click()\n  const props = await getProps(page)\n  expect(props.value).toBe(\"new\")\n})\n```\n\n### **Pattern: Form Validation**\n```javascript\ntest(\"validation errors appear\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.locator('[data-pw-input]').fill(\"invalid\")\n  await page.locator('[data-pw-input]').blur()\n  await syncLV(page)\n  \n  await expect(page.locator('[data-pw-error]')).toBeVisible()\n  await expect(page.locator('[data-pw-is-valid]')).toHaveText(\"Valid: false\")\n})\n```\n\n### **Pattern: Stream Operations**\n```javascript\ntest(\"adds item to stream\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.fill('[data-testid=\"name-input\"]', \"New Item\")\n  await page.click('[data-testid=\"add-button\"]')\n  await syncLV(page)\n  \n  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid=\"item-4\"]')).toBeVisible()\n  const heading = page.locator('h3:has-text(\"Items\")')\n  await expect(heading).toHaveText(\"Items (4)\")\n})\n```\n\n### **Pattern: Event Reply (Request/Response)**\n```javascript\ntest(\"event reply data received\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.locator('[data-pw-fetch-user-1]').click()\n  await syncLV(page)\n  \n  await expect(page.locator('[data-pw-user-data]')).toContainText('\"name\":\"John\"')\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. CONFIGURATION & CONVENTIONS\n\n**In mix.exs:**\n- `elixirc_paths: [..., \"test/e2e/features/*/\"]` - Compiles all feature LiveView modules\n\n**Environment:**\n```bash\nMIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs  # Starts server\nnpm run e2e:test                              # Runs tests against server\n```\n\n**Browser Testing:**\n- Only Chromium enabled (Firefox/Safari commented out)\n- Traces & screenshots on failure\n- Health check at `http://localhost:4004/health`\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe E2E test structure is **feature-centric and colocated**, with each feature containing:\n1. **LiveView module** (`live.ex`) - Server logic\n2. **Vue component(s)** (`.vue`) - Client UI\n3. **Playwright spec** (`.spec.js`) - Test scenarios\n4. **Optional controller** (for dead view patterns)\n\nTests follow **arrange-act-assert** with **syncLV() synchronization** between page interactions and assertions. The setup leverages Vite for component bundling, Phoenix for routing/state, and Playwright for automation—all coordinated through a shared `window.liveSocket` reference."}],"totalDurationMs":64032,"totalTokens":64620,"totalToolUseCount":24,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3072,"cache_read_input_tokens":56738,"output_tokens":4807,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3072,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}}}}
