{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011iPYNtgaP5YP8GYaRoKXqK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create all the React component and test files. Let me look at how `live` prop is passed in the React renderer to understand the API surface for `pushEvent`.\n\nLooking at the React renderer code in `renderers/react.ts:35-39`, I see props are spread with `...state.props` and `live: ctx.hook`. The `live` prop is the hook instance itself. So in React components, `props.live.pushEvent(...)` is how you push events. But also `useLive()` returns the hook from context.\n\nLet me create all the React components and their corresponding LiveView modules."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":101003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":319},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"4fe6c921-ef15-4a04-90fb-e23557958d0c"}
