{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation to capture all important details.\n\n1. The user's task is US-015: Add React E2E tests for basic features. The task says \"As a maintainer, I want E2E tests for React covering the same basic scenarios as existing Vue tests.\"\n\n2. I started by exploring the existing Vue E2E test structure and the React renderer implementation using Task agents.\n\n3. I read the key infrastructure files:\n   - test/e2e/js/app.js - Vue-only setup using createLiveVite and getHooks\n   - test/e2e/vite.config.js - Vue-only vite config\n   - test/e2e/test_helper.exs - Elixir test server with routes\n   - test/e2e/utils.js - syncLV, evalLV, randomString helpers\n   - assets/renderers/react.ts - React renderer implementation\n   - assets/useReact.ts - React hooks (useLive, useLiveEventReact, useLiveNavigationReact)\n   - assets/index.ts - Exports\n   - assets/hooks.ts - getMultiRendererHook, getRendererHook, getVueHook\n   - lib/live_vite.ex - LiveVite.vue and LiveVite.react functions\n   - lib/live_vite/components.ex - Component discovery\n\n4. I read all Vue E2E feature files to understand what to replicate:\n   - basic/ - Counter with increment\n   - event/ - useLiveEvent for server events\n   - navigation/ - useLiveNavigation for routing\n   - slot/ - Non-ASCII slot content\n   - stream/ - LiveView streams\n   - event-reply/ - useEventReply (Vue-only, no React equivalent)\n   - prop-diff/ - JSON patch diffing\n\n5. Key findings:\n   - LiveVite.react() sets v-framework=\"react\" and delegates to vue()\n   - The rendered div gets data-framework=\"react\" attribute\n   - getMultiRendererHook dispatches based on data-framework attribute\n   - useEventReply is Vue-only (no React equivalent) - so I skipped event-reply tests\n   - React renderer passes props directly + `live` prop for hook instance\n   - Slots are passed as React elements via dangerouslySetInnerHTML\n\n6. Files I created/modified:\n\n   a. Modified test/e2e/js/app.js - Changed from Vue-only getHooks to getMultiRendererHook with both Vue and React renderers\n   \n   b. Modified test/e2e/vite.config.js - Added @vitejs/plugin-react, added react/react-dom aliases, added include pattern for tsx/jsx\n   \n   c. Installed @vitejs/plugin-react as devDependency\n   \n   d. Created 6 React E2E feature directories with 3 files each (live.ex, component.tsx, spec.js):\n      - react-basic/ - counter.tsx, live.ex, react-basic.spec.js\n      - react-event/ - event_test.tsx, live.ex, react-event.spec.js\n      - react-navigation/ - navigation.tsx, live.ex, react-navigation.spec.js\n      - react-slot/ - slot_test.tsx, live.ex, react-slot.spec.js\n      - react-stream/ - stream_test.tsx, live.ex, react-stream.spec.js\n      - react-prop-diff/ - prop-display.tsx, live.ex, react-prop-diff.spec.js\n   \n   e. Modified test/e2e/test_helper.exs - Added React routes and updated live_reload pattern to include tsx/jsx\n\n7. Vite build succeeded with the new React setup.\n\n8. When trying to run E2E tests, I encountered several issues:\n   - mix not in PATH - needed nix-shell\n   - Erlang/OTP version mismatch when using nix store elixir directly\n   - E2E server dying because stdin closed (test_helper.exs reads stdin to know when to stop)\n   - Fixed by using `sleep infinity | MIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs`\n   - Playwright browsers not installed - installed them\n   - Missing system libraries for Chromium on NixOS (libglib, libgbm, etc.)\n   - Tried various approaches: nix-shell with libraries, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS\n   - Still failing due to Chromium not being able to find shared libraries on NixOS\n\n9. Current state: The E2E server is running (background task bff093a), health check works. But Playwright can't launch Chromium because the NixOS system doesn't have the native libraries that the npm-downloaded Chromium binary needs. The nix-provided playwright-browsers have different versions (1155 and 1194) while npm playwright expects v1181.\n\n10. The user has not provided any feedback yet - only the initial task request.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's task is **US-015: Add React E2E tests for basic features**. The exact requirement: \"As a maintainer, I want E2E tests for React covering the same basic scenarios as existing Vue tests.\" Upon completion, signal with `<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Phoenix LiveView + Vue.js/React integration library (LiveVite)\n   - Multi-framework renderer pattern: `getMultiRendererHook()` dispatches based on `data-framework` DOM attribute\n   - `LiveVite.react()` sets `v-framework=\"react\"` then delegates to `vue()` rendering pipeline\n   - React renderer uses `createRoot`/`hydrateRoot`, re-renders full tree on prop/slot updates\n   - React hooks: `useLive()`, `useLiveEventReact()`, `useLiveNavigationReact()` from `live_vite`\n   - Slots in React: passed as props (functions returning React elements via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`)\n   - `useEventReply` is Vue-only — no React equivalent exists, so event-reply tests were skipped\n   - Playwright E2E testing with Phoenix server, `syncLV()` for LiveView synchronization\n   - NixOS environment: Node.js/Elixir via `nix-shell`, Playwright browser deps issue\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **test/e2e/js/app.js** (MODIFIED) — Changed from Vue-only `getHooks(liveViteApp)` to multi-renderer setup with `getMultiRendererHook`:\n     ```javascript\n     import \"phoenix_html\"\n     import { Socket } from \"phoenix\"\n     import { LiveSocket } from \"phoenix_live_view\"\n     import { getMultiRendererHook, createVueRenderer, createReactRenderer, findComponent } from \"live_vite\"\n     import { h } from \"vue\"\n     import \"vite/modulepreload-polyfill\"\n\n     const vueRenderer = createVueRenderer({\n       setup: (createApp, component, props, slots, plugin, el) => {\n         const app = createApp({ render: () => h(component, props, slots) })\n         app.use(plugin)\n         app.mount(el)\n         return app\n       },\n     })\n     const vueComponents = import.meta.glob(\"../features/**/*.vue\", { eager: true })\n     const reactRenderer = createReactRenderer()\n     const reactComponents = import.meta.glob(\"../features/**/*.tsx\", { eager: true })\n\n     const VueHook = getMultiRendererHook({\n       vue: {\n         renderer: vueRenderer,\n         resolve: name => findComponent(vueComponents, name),\n       },\n       react: {\n         renderer: reactRenderer,\n         resolve: name => findComponent(reactComponents, name),\n       },\n     })\n\n     let csrfToken = document.querySelector(\"meta[name='csrf-token']\")?.getAttribute(\"content\")\n     let liveSocket = new LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n       params: { _csrf_token: csrfToken },\n       hooks: { VueHook },\n     })\n     liveSocket.connect()\n     window.liveSocket = liveSocket\n     ```\n\n   - **test/e2e/vite.config.js** (MODIFIED) — Added React plugin and aliases:\n     ```javascript\n     import react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\"\n     // ...\n     plugins: [vue(), react({ include: /\\.(tsx|jsx)$/ })],\n     resolve: {\n       alias: {\n         vue: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../node_modules/vue\"),\n         react: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../node_modules/react\"),\n         \"react-dom\": path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../node_modules/react-dom\"),\n         \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\"),\n         live_vite: path.resolve(__dirname, \"../../assets/index.ts\"),\n       },\n     },\n     ```\n\n   - **test/e2e/test_helper.exs** (MODIFIED) — Added React routes and tsx pattern:\n     ```elixir\n     # Added to live_session routes:\n     live \"/react-test\", ReactTestLive\n     live \"/react-prop-diff-test\", ReactPropDiffTestLive\n     live \"/react-navigation/:page\", ReactNavigationLive\n     live \"/react-navigation/alt/:page\", ReactNavigationLive\n     live \"/react-events\", ReactEventLive\n     live \"/react-streams\", ReactStreamLive\n     live \"/react-slot-test\", ReactSlotTestLive\n     ```\n     Also updated live_reload pattern: `~r\"test/e2e/features/.*\\.(ex|exs|vue|js|ts|tsx|jsx)$\"`\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-basic/counter.tsx** (CREATED) — React counter component using `useLive()` hook with `useState` for diff slider and `live.pushEvent(\"increment\", { value: diff })`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-basic/live.ex** (CREATED) — `LiveVite.E2E.ReactTestLive` module, same logic as Vue TestLive but using `<LiveVite.react>` instead of `<LiveVite.vue>`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-basic/react-basic.spec.js** (CREATED) — Playwright test matching Vue basic test: verifies counter rendering, slider, and increment events.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-event/event_test.tsx** (CREATED) — React component using `useLive()` and `useLiveEventReact()` for notification and custom events, with `useState` for input tracking and event accumulation.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-event/live.ex** (CREATED) — `LiveVite.E2E.ReactEventLive`, identical logic to Vue EventLive but renders with `<LiveVite.react>`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-event/react-event.spec.js** (CREATED) — 4 tests matching Vue event tests: notification events, custom events, mixed events, rapid sequential events.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-navigation/navigation.tsx** (CREATED) — React component using `useLiveNavigationReact()` with `patch()` and `navigate()`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-navigation/live.ex** (CREATED) — `LiveVite.E2E.ReactNavigationLive`, handles params and query params, renders with `<LiveVite.react>`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-navigation/react-navigation.spec.js** (CREATED) — 2 tests: patch query params + navigate between routes, direct route access with params.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-slot/slot_test.tsx** (CREATED) — React component receiving `default` slot prop (a function returning React element):\n     ```tsx\n     interface Props {\n       label?: string\n       default?: () => any\n     }\n     export default function SlotTest({ label, default: defaultSlot }: Props) {\n       return (\n         <div className=\"slot-test\">\n           {label && <span data-pw-label>{label}</span>}\n           <div data-pw-slot>{defaultSlot ? defaultSlot() : null}</div>\n         </div>\n       )\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-slot/live.ex** (CREATED) — `LiveVite.E2E.ReactSlotTestLive`, renders 5 slot instances with non-ASCII content using `<LiveVite.react>`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-slot/react-slot.spec.js** (CREATED) — Tests for Polish, Japanese, Emoji, Mixed scripts, and Special Latin characters in slots.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-stream/stream_test.tsx** (CREATED) — Full React stream component with add/remove/clear/reset/limit operations using `useLive()` and `useState`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-stream/live.ex** (CREATED) — `LiveVite.E2E.ReactStreamLive`, identical stream logic to Vue StreamLive.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-stream/react-stream.spec.js** (CREATED) — Complete stream test suite (14+ tests including limit operations).\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-prop-diff/prop-display.tsx** (CREATED) — Simple React component displaying `JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-prop-diff/live.ex** (CREATED) — `LiveVite.E2E.ReactPropDiffTestLive`, identical prop-diff logic to Vue PropDiffTestLive using `<LiveVite.react>`.\n\n   - **test/e2e/features/react-prop-diff/react-prop-diff.spec.js** (CREATED) — 16 tests covering all prop diff scenarios.\n\n   - **package.json** — `@vitejs/plugin-react` was installed as devDependency.\n\n   Key reference files read but not modified:\n   - `assets/renderers/react.ts` — React renderer implementation (createReactRenderer)\n   - `assets/useReact.ts` — React hooks (useLive, useLiveEventReact, useLiveNavigationReact)\n   - `assets/hooks.ts` — getMultiRendererHook implementation\n   - `lib/live_vite.ex` — LiveVite.react/vue functions\n   - `assets/index.ts` — Export map\n   - All Vue E2E feature files for reference\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Vite build warnings about externalized modules** (react-dom/server): Just warnings, not errors. SSR modules (util, crypto, async_hooks, stream) externalized for browser. Build succeeded.\n   - **`mix` not in PATH**: Needed `nix-shell -p elixir nodejs` to run mix commands.\n   - **Erlang/OTP version mismatch**: Using nix store elixir directly with OTP 28 caused Hex.State module load error. Fixed by using `nix-shell -p elixir` which provides matching OTP 27.\n   - **E2E server dying immediately**: `test_helper.exs` reads stdin and shuts down on EOF. Background processes had stdin closed. Fixed by piping `sleep infinity` into the command: `sleep infinity | MIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs`.\n   - **Playwright browsers not installed**: Ran `npx playwright install chromium` to download.\n   - **Missing system libraries for Chromium on NixOS** (ONGOING): The npm-downloaded Chromium binary needs native libraries (libglib, libgbm, libnspr, libnss, etc.) that NixOS doesn't have in standard paths. Tried:\n     - `nix-shell` with library packages — libraries are installed but not on LD_LIBRARY_PATH\n     - Setting `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` from `NIX_LDFLAGS` — partially worked (found glib) but `libgbm.so.1` still missing (mesa doesn't export it in the expected path)\n     - `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS=true` — skipped the pre-check but Chromium still can't load libraries\n     - `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` with nix playwright-driver.browsers — version mismatch (nix has v1155/v1194, npm playwright 1.54.1 expects v1181)\n     - This is still unresolved.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Completed**: All React component files, LiveView modules, test specs, app.js multi-renderer setup, vite config, routes, and Vite build.\n   - **Ongoing**: Cannot run Playwright E2E tests on this NixOS system due to Chromium native library dependencies. The E2E server is confirmed running (health check passes at http://127.0.0.1:4004). The Vite build succeeds. The issue is purely the Playwright/Chromium browser execution environment.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message: \"## Task: US-015: Add React E2E tests for basic features\\nAs a maintainer, I want E2E tests for React covering the same basic scenarios as existing Vue tests.\\n\\nWhen finished, signal completion with:\\n<promise>COMPLETE</promise>\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Successfully run the React E2E tests to verify they pass (blocked by Playwright/Chromium NixOS library issue)\n   - Potentially verify existing Vue E2E tests still pass with the multi-renderer app.js change\n   - Signal completion with `<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   All code has been written and the Vite build succeeds. I was actively trying to run the Playwright E2E tests but am blocked by NixOS not having the native shared libraries (libglib-2.0.so.0, libgbm.so.1, etc.) that Playwright's bundled Chromium needs. The E2E server is running in background (task bff093a, started with `nix-shell -p elixir nodejs --run \"bash -c 'sleep infinity | MIX_ENV=e2e mix run test/e2e/test_helper.exs'\"`).\n\n   Last attempted command:\n   ```\n   nix-shell -p nodejs chromium glib nspr nss dbus.lib atk at-spi2-atk expat at-spi2-core xorg.libX11 xorg.libXcomposite xorg.libXdamage xorg.libXext xorg.libXfixes xorg.libXrandr mesa xorg.libxcb libxkbcommon systemdLibs alsa-lib cups.lib cairo pango gobject-introspection --run '\n     export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$(echo $NIX_LDFLAGS | tr \" \" \"\\n\" | grep \"^-L\" | sed \"s/^-L//\" | tr \"\\n\" \":\"):$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\n     export PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALID