{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyzYWXpRLVodw43uzxAmFQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have the full implementation. Here's what I found:\n\n## `findComponent` Function Implementation\n\n**Location:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/utils.ts` (lines 35-79)\n\n**Export:** `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/index.ts` (line 27)\n\n### Full Implementation:\n\n```typescript\nexport const findComponent = (components: ComponentMap, name: string): ComponentOrComponentPromise => {\n  const nameParts = name.replace(/\\.vue$/, '').split('/').filter(part => part !== 'index')\n  const matches: [string, ComponentOrComponentPromise][] = []\n\n  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(components)) {\n    let keyParts = key.split('/')\n    \n    if (keyParts[keyParts.length - 1] === 'index.vue') {\n      keyParts = keyParts.slice(0, -1)\n    } else {\n      keyParts[keyParts.length - 1] = keyParts[keyParts.length - 1].replace(/\\.vue$/, '')\n    }\n    \n    if (nameParts.length <= keyParts.length) {\n      let isMatch = true\n      for (let i = 0; i < nameParts.length; i++) {\n        const keyPart = keyParts[keyParts.length - nameParts.length + i]\n        if (nameParts[i] !== keyPart) {\n          isMatch = false\n          break\n        }\n      }\n      \n      if (isMatch) {\n        matches.push([key, value])\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (matches.length === 1) return matches[0][1]\n\n  if (matches.length > 1) {\n    const matchList = matches.map(([key]) => key).join('\\n')\n    throw new Error(`Component '${name}' is ambiguous. Found multiple matches:\\n\\n${matchList}\\n\\n`)\n  }\n\n  // a helpful message for the user\n  const availableComponents = Object.keys(components)\n    .map(key => key.replace(\"../../lib/\", \"\").replace(\"/index.vue\", \"\").replace(\".vue\", \"\").replace(\"./\", \"\"))\n    .filter(key => !key.startsWith(\"_build\"))\n    .join(\"\\n\")\n\n  throw new Error(`Component '${name}' not found! Available components:\\n\\n${availableComponents}\\n\\n`)\n}\n```\n\n### How It Works:\n\n1. **Input Processing**: Takes a component name and removes `.vue` extension, then splits by `/` and filters out `index` parts\n   - Example: `\"Form/Input.vue\"` → `[\"Form\", \"Input\"]`\n\n2. **Glob Matching**: Iterates through all component entries from the glob-provided `ComponentMap`:\n   - Splits each key by `/`\n   - Normalizes paths by handling `index.vue` files (removes the filename, keeps the directory)\n   - Removes `.vue` extensions from regular component files\n\n3. **Suffix Matching**: Checks if the name parts match the **end** of the key parts (suffix matching):\n   - Uses array index alignment: `keyParts[keyParts.length - nameParts.length + i]`\n   - This allows matching `\"Input\"` to `\"Form/Input\"` or `\"components/Form/Input\"`\n\n4. **Resolution**:\n   - **Exact match (1 result)**: Returns the component\n   - **Multiple matches**: Throws an ambiguity error listing all matches\n   - **No match**: Throws an error listing all available components (with cleaned paths)\n\nThis approach enables flexible component resolution where you can refer to components by their short name (`\"Button\"`) or partial path (`\"Form/Input\"`) and it will find them regardless of where they're located in the directory structure."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4b91fa (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 19672\ntool_uses: 2\nduration_ms: 9931</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"e335696c-219e-4f77-b521-2bd85456d2c1","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the file `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/utils.ts` and look for the `findComponent` function. Also check `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/index.ts` for the export of findComponent. I need to understand how it resolves component name