{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01A1nQRyHFBCk8FijufwuFf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait, let me re-read the renderer code more carefully. Let me look at `renderComponent` again:\n\n```typescript\nfunction renderComponent(state: RendererState<ReactRendererState>): void {\n  const { root, component, hook } = state.app!\n  const inner = createElement(component as any, {\n    ...state.props,\n    ...mapValues(state.slots, slotFn => slotFn()),\n    live: hook,\n  })\n```\n\nAnd `state.slots` comes from `htmlSlotsToReact`:\n```typescript\nfunction htmlSlotsToReact(slots: Record<string, string>): Record<string, () => any> {\n  return mapValues(slots, html => () =>\n    createElement(\"span\", { dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: html.trim() } })\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSo `state.slots` = `{ default: () => createElement(\"span\", ...) }` (functions).\nAnd `mapValues(state.slots, slotFn => slotFn())` calls each function, producing `{ default: <span element> }`.\n\nSo the component receives `default` as a React element (JSX element), not a function. My fix above (using `defaultSlot` as a value, not calling it) should be correct.\n\nLet me rebuild and test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":99146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"18f02e98-4725-4011-b492-6f72c2fc41a8"}
