{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01T1qduh8M5G49MUjLghB2U7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The original config doesn't have `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` support in the playwright config (I added that). So it falls back to the playwright-bundled Chromium which doesn't work on NixOS. This confirms the Vue E2E tests **have never been run on this NixOS machine** — they were designed to run in CI (Ubuntu).\n\nSo the Vue test failures I saw earlier are due to: my `check_origin: false` and `type=\"module\"` changes. The `type=\"module\"` change broke the Vue tests because the script is placed inside the LiveView container and when LiveView patches the DOM during websocket connection, module scripts don't re-execute.\n\nActually wait — the script is in the \"live\" layout, which is rendered on the initial HTTP response before the WebSocket connects. The browser should execute `<script type=\"module\">` during initial page load. Let me think more carefully...\n\nThe issue is that `<script>` (without `type=\"module\"`) is a blocking script — it loads synchronously. `<script type=\"module\">` is always deferred. This means the JS loads after the DOM is parsed, and the LiveSocket connection happens after the script executes. This should still work.\n\nBut the counter div had `<!---->` content, meaning Vue mounted but rendered nothing. Let me pop my stash, keep the original `outDir` fix and `check_origin` fix, but investigate the Vue empty render issue more carefully."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1774,"cache_read_input_tokens":128629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1774},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5cbf92b-6106-41f2-ab9b-5f76d18aa231","uuid":"8cce9653-ad92-401f-a55f-4ae82f