ok()` (single-renderer shorthand) + `getVueHook()` (legacy Vue-specific)\n- `assets/server.ts` - `getRendererRender()` (framework-agnostic SSR) + `getRender()` (legacy Vue SSR)\n- All existing Vue APIs preserved for backward compatibility\n- Elixir `live_vite.ex` renders `data-framework=\"vue\"` on component div\n\n## Key Patterns\n- Hook stores renderer state as `this.vue` (even for non-Vue renderers, for backward compat)\n- Hook stores active renderer as `this.__renderer` for use in updated/destroyed lifecycle\n- `getMultiRendererHook(renderers)` dispatches based on `data-framework` DOM attribute\n- Single-renderer fallback: if only one renderer registered, `data-framework` attribute is optional\n- Slots flow as raw HTML strings to the renderer; renderer converts to framework-specific format\n- Props parsed from DOM attributes are plain objects; renderer wraps in its reactivity system\n- JSON Patch library (`jsonPatch.ts`) is framework-agnostic, operates on plain objects\n- Elixir test failures for SSR NodeJS and installer tests are pre-existing (Node.js not in nix-shell PATH)\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":21,"oldLines":3,"newStart":21,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - Props parsed from DOM attributes are plain objects; renderer wraps in its reactivity system"," - JSON Patch library (`jsonPatch.ts`) is framework-agnostic, operates on plain objects"," - Elixir test failures for SSR NodeJS and installer tests are pre-existing (Node.js not in nix-shell PATH)","+- E2E Vite build: run `npx vite build --config test/e2e/vite.config.js` from project root (not from test/e2e/)","+- E2E test_helper.exs: needs `check_origin: false` and `<script type=\"module\">` for Playwright testing","+- Playwright on NixOS: use `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` env var with nix chromium + `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS=1`","+- `findComponent` updated to handle .vue/.tsx/.jsx/.ts/.js extensions (was .vue only)","+- When using `getMultiRendererHook`, resolve functions must unwr